\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. In loving-kindness Jesus came,
\par My soul in mercy to reclaim,
\par And from the depths of sin and shame
\par Through grace He lifted me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par From sinking sand He lifted me;
\par With tender hand He lifted me;
\par From shades of night to plains of light,
\par O praise His name, He lifted me!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. He called me long before I heard,
\par Before my sinful heart was stirred;
\par But when I took Him at His word,
\par Forgiven He lifted me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par From sinking sand He lifted me;
\par With tender hand He lifted me;
\par From shades of night to plains of light,
\par O praise His name, He lifted me!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. His brow was pierced with many a thorn,
\par His hands by cruel nails were torn,
\par When from my guilt and grief, forlorn,
\par In love He lifted me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par From sinking sand He lifted me;
\par With tender hand He lifted me;
\par From shades of night to plains of light,
\par O praise His name, He lifted me!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Now on a higher plane I dwell,
\par And with my soul I know 'tis well;
\par Yet how or why, cannot tell,
\par He should have lifted me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par From sinking sand He lifted me;
\par With tender hand He lifted me;
\par From shades of night to plains of light,
\par O praise His name, He lifted me!
\par \f1 
